Architecture Decision: Flat Binary via .S + C Preprocessor

Since you're rejecting ELF (correct call — ELF headers are a known attack surface and the PT_NOTE segment has been used for persistence), the approach is:

Flat binary — raw opcodes, no headers, loaded by LILO directly at a physical address. LILO can load a flat binary as a "other=" stanza, not just "image=". The preprocessor (cpp) runs on your .S file before GAS assembles it, giving you #define, #include, #ifdef — full macro capability — with zero ELF overhead.
